# symbolic SATO template
# family: CrossOver (label-type-code=6) / 2x7.25 / manual, 2-up kiss-cut
# ported field-for-field from c:\Workspace\southalr\t0sz2x725-co-man-2upkiss.i (operator-
# triggered path, dispatched from dtlbl061.p:767 [SAP] / dtlbl071.p:738 [Non-SAP] when
# ih-label-type-code=6 -- confirmed still in production use by Shringa Sekhar/Sachin
# Santhosam, 2026-09-11).
#
# "2-up kiss-cut" = two copies of the same label content printed side by side on one
# physical stock, perforated but not separated -- the legacy .i file below is genuinely
# the ref-first content duplicated at a second, offset coordinate set, not a rendering
# trick. Right-hand copy (H0800/0785/0783.../0468) plus left-hand copy (H0394/0379/
# 0377.../0062, coordinate-for-coordinate identical to lt06_xover_2x725_ref-first.sato's
# field positions).
#
# Differences from the automatic (ref-first/ref-last) path, all intentional/verbatim from
# source, not oversights:
# - Heat/speed defaults #E2/CS4 (vs the auto path's #F5/CS6) -- same "no setsato table
#   equivalent" gap already accepted elsewhere in this port.
# - An extra \x1bEX0 (buffer-extend) command and a longer \x1bA114710828 positioning
#   command in the header, neither present in the auto path.
# - Barcode-setup command is \x1bDH02136 (with all 4 UPC fields incl. check digit) instead
#   of the auto path's \x1bBLH02136 (3 fields, check digit commented out in source).
# - Date field uses the full {MfgDateCode} (yjjj:HHmm) here, not {MfgDateCodeShort} --
#   the manual .i file appends timstr (HHmm) after the colon; the auto ref-first/ref-last
#   files don't.
# - In real Progress, LabelVarB is empty and the trailing "ESC Q<qty> ESC Z" is appended by
#   the *calling* program (dtlbl061.p line 767-769) generically for every label type, using
#   the operator-entered prt-qty -- not hardcoded to 1 like the PLC path's ESC Q1. Folded
#   into this template directly (as the Quantity placeholder below) to match this port's
#   one-file-per-template convention; functionally identical to the split-across-two-places
#   legacy source.
#
# Same sapitemhdr-vs-itemdet approximation as the auto variants for prt-co-desc-us/fr/sp
# and prt-shape-co-desc/prt-shape-co-d -- see lt06_xover_2x725_ref-first.sato's header.

<STX>
\x1bA
\x1bEX0
\x1bA3V+000H+024
\x1bCS4
\x1b#E2
\x1bA114710828
\x1bZ
<ETX>
<STX>
